n Dubuffet previously located in front of the James R. Thompson Center in the Loop community area of Chicago, Illinois.","Monument with Standing Beast"],"15730925":["Group of Four Trees is an abstract outdoor sculpture completed in 1972 by the French artist Jean Dubuffet.","Group of Four Trees (Jean Dubuffet)"],"16952279":["Courre Merlan (Whiting Chase) is an oil painting by French artist Jean Dubuffet. It has been at the Indianapolis Museum of Art since 1992.","Courre Merlan (Whiting Chase)"],"18844630":["Jardin d'émail (1968-1974) also known as Enamel garden is an outdoor sculpture in the Kröller-Müller Museum in Otterlo, The Netherlands. The sculpture was created by artist Jean Dubuffet.","Jardin d'émail"],"18880407":["Monument au Fantôme is an outdoor sculpture by French sculptor Jean Dubuffet, in 1977. It was originally inaugurated at the plaza of 1100 Louisiana.","Monument au Fantôme"],"19887181":["The Cow with the Subtile Nose is an oil and enamel painting on canvas by French painter Jean Dubuffet, created in 1954. It is held in the Museum of Modern Art, in New York.","The Cow with the Subtile Nose"],"60675985":["Jazz Band (Dirty Style Blues) is an oil on canvas painting by French artist Jean Dubuffet, from 1944. It depicts the six members of a jazz orchestra.","Jazz Band (Dirty Style Blues)"],"99898240":["Cows and Groomers is an oil painting on canvas by the French artist Jean Dubuffet, dated from August 1943. It is held in the collection of the Unterlinden Museum in Colmar, Alsace.","Cows and Groomers"],"120435142":["Hotel du Cantal is an oil on canvas painting by the French painter Jean Dubuffet, created in 1961. The work, part of a major donation made by the artist in 1967, is held at the Musée des Arts Décoratifs, in Paris.","Hotel du Cantal"]},"titlesFrom":["fr","P1476","alias:en","alias:fr","aliasFilter:1"]}